WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.434
-Returning to the stage.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.367
-Yes. "Comedian and writer."
I like that.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:05.734
-Yeah, me too.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.567
-I guess my people said,
"Throw in writer,

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.234
so people will think
he's like, oh, you know?"

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:12.067
-Oh, my God. This is exciting.
You on the stage.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.367
You're the new "Funny Girl."

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:16.968
You're replacing Lea Michele
in "Funny Girl."

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.701
Is that what
we're talking about?

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.400
This is "Small Talk."
-Yeah.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.100
-Are you -- I'm trying to think.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.968
Do you like small talk?
-I love small talk.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:28.834
I'm great at -- My whole life,
I talk to everybody.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.801
You -- I mean, I feel like
you're kind of like that, too,

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:32.701
like a friendly type person.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:35.400
-I go in the store, you know,
you have a little conversation.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.667
Little --
"Eh, you know what I mean?

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.968
I shouldn't...

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.501
Little much on the holidays.
I ate too much."

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:43.901
And they're like, "Ah, ha ha."

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.434
You have a little,
you know, bonding moment.

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:47.400
-You do those things. You throw
little bonding moments.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.000
-I feel like you do that, too,
with people.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.834
-I do a little bit.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:53.567
You almost sound defensive.
It's a positive quality.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.767
-Defensive?
-You did.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.033
His voice when he --
He goes, "I do!"

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.367
Your voice went up like, "Hey!"

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:01.767
-You know what I keep
thinking of?

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.501
Do you remember back when we
were on "Saturday Night Live" --

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.200
You were always very nice to me,
by the way.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.167
I consider you -- The whole
reason I have this show is you.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.367
-What? [ Laughs ]
-But, anyways, uh...

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:13.434
No. You know what
I was thinking of?

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:16.000
Do you remember when --
-I almost believed it.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.968
-But when we would go get tea
at, like, 2:00 in the morning?

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:20.133
-Yes, exactly.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.801
-We'd go to this deli,
this bodega.

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.701
-Yeah, the bodega,
and that guy was a ju--

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:27.367
That guy was an Olympic
judo champion, according to him.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:28.634
I'm sure he could just say it.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.267
-How do you know all this
about this guy?

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.200
-From small talk.
-Small talk.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.200
But I remember we were going,
and somebody yells --

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.467
Because walking with Colin Quinn

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.934
in New York City
is like the mayor.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.467
He was like,
"Colin! Yo, Colin Quinn!

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:40.767
Come on back to Brooklyn, man!"

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.467
-It's like a bad commercial.
Like, "Hey, pal."

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:46.400
-No. I remember the guy goes,
"Yo, Colin, come here!"

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.100
And you go, "You come here."

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.400
-Yeah, because that was,
like, a power move.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.033
The guy's like, "Hey, Colin."
-Yeah.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.901
-He wasn't do anything
that couldn't be --

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.801
He's, like, calling me over.
Why are you taking his side?

00:01:57.801 --> 00:01:59.267
You don't even know the guy.

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:01.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.534
Crowd's like,
"You sound like a real ehh."

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.467
They called me over.
You don't call me over here.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:07.701
-"No, you come over here.
Yeah, what are you doing?"

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:10.200
-But here's the thing
about "Small Talk."

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.834
It's, um...

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:14.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.667
Is that -- It is.
It's about being friendly.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:19.801
And it's so funny to me
because one of the criticisms

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.868
you always hear is,
"Oh, Jimmy's so enthusiastic,

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:25.133
so friendly with his guests."

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.133
It's like, "Yeah,
what is he supposed to...?"

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.667
You're supposed to
bring 'em out.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:31.133
"Hey, I heard your new movie.
Yeah. Sounds like it sucks."

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:32.334
You know what I mean?

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.667
-I can't do that.
-No, you can't.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.467
Gotta be nice.
-No, exactly, yeah.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:38.734
Without movies and TV,
I wouldn't have a show.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.467
-Exactly.
-I want them all to work.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.167
-People think sullen is so hip.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:43.634
Well, guess what.
I don't buy it.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.834
Musicians are different.
You're allowed to be sullen.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:48.767
Different vibe.
But I'm talking about in comedy.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.701
-I'm talking about this guy.
I'm talking about "Small Talk."

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.567
But I'm also talking
about this guy.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:56.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:56.133 --> 00:03:00.067
Dude, what?! What in the world?
Who is this?

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.667
Who is this?
-Give me a break.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.734
-Who is this?!

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.467
What porno is this from?

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:07.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:12.467
-I was hung over.
-A calendar or something?

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.834
You're very good-looking.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.434
-Did you see the new
Chippendales show?

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:17.601
-You're a very good-looking guy.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.067
-I really was.
That was a great picture.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:20.634
The guy was just
a hungover friend of mine.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.400
He had a camera
and he took a picture.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.934
They needed pictures
in those days.

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.868
You go out, and you
hand around your pictures.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:27.100
-Of course.
-You know what I mean?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.634
-Yeah, to get auditions
and stuff like that.

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:30.367
-Yeah, stuff like that.
-Any big movies

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.000
that you ever auditioned for
you didn't get?

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.033
-Well, Tom Cruise, "Cocktail."
Which, you see that picture --

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.334
I don't know how
I couldn't get it.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.067
I auditioned for "Cocktail,"
but I did --

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:40.534
I was a bartender,
so I was like,

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:42.067
"I'm gonna do
a little stage business."

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:43.334
You know what I mean?

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.400
So, I show up at the audition.
I met Tom Cruise.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.968
I was kind of -- I was still
starstruck a little bit.

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.767
You know, Tom Cruise. I didn't
know he was going to be there.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.234
-Yeah.
-So I start doing the thing

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.267
where I'm the other bartender,
if you saw the movie.

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:53.968
Nobody did.
It was a horrible movie.

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:55.901
[ Laughter ]
-It was a good movie.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.267
-What do you mean, a good movie?

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.767
It's one of the worst movies
of all time.

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.968
People write about you --
you're too enthusiastic.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.267
-You can't say that to me.
I like that.

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:07.334
Hippy hippy shake.
-Oh, the worst.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:09.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:11.534
I auditioned for the bartender.
I didn't know.

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:13.534
The fix is in
in all these things.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.467
Like idiots, you show up at
the audition. But I show up --

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:19.000
-Fix is in.
-Fix is in.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.400
And I start doing, like,
pantomime bartending.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.501
I used to be a bartender,
so it wasn't that --

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.300
I'm like this --
-Is Tom Cruise there?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.934
-Yeah. I sucked the energy
out of the room so bad.

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:32.400
Because I was always --

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.000
I was a terrible actor,
and I was also doing,

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.033
like, mime --
pretending to bartend.

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:39.534
And I was making drinks.
Like, just straining them.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:43.067
-"Get out of here, dude."
You were straining the drinks?

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:44.868
-They were like -- They couldn't
wait for it to end.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.501
It was just so horrible.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.300
-That's so funny.
-I did what nobody could do.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.601
I wiped the smile off
Tom Cruise's face.

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.267
I swear to God.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.000
Because he came in --
-Like, "This is not funny.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.701
This is a waste of my time."
-He's all smiling.

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.200
Charming guy, you know?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.000
By the time --
He's like, "Okay, thanks, man."

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.234
Somebody calls you "man"
at an audition,

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.400
It's usually
they don't like you.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.400
-You were almost in a movie
with Mike Myers.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.300
Offered you a role.
-That was the famous one, yeah.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.434
I was supposed to be
in "Austin Powers."

00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:16.834
But he called me up
and literally said,

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:18.033
"You got the part."

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.567
And I go, "No, Mike,
I don't want the part."

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.534
For no reason.

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:24.934
-I was gonna be Scott Evil,
the son.

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:28.100
'Cause he saw me on --
he saw me on "Larry Sanders,"

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.267
and he was like,
"Do what you did with Rip Torn.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.801
Be the son."

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:34.634
All three of them.
-You don't want to be in that.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.701
You wouldn't have wanted
to do that.

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.801
-Exactly.
-Look at what you're doing now.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.534
-Why be in a franchise
of movies?

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:42.501
-Then everyone's yelling,
"Scott Evil,"

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.167
when you're crossing the street.
-Yeah.

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:45.901
-Now they're like, "Colin Quinn.
What's up? 'Small Talk.'"

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.601
-"Scott Evil.
Scott Evil, come over here."

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.734
"You come here."
-"No, you come here, buddy."

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:52.367
Yeah, exactly.
I think you made the right move.

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:53.868
-Oh, thanks.

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:57.367
-'Cause I think this man would
be proud of what you're doing.

00:05:57.367 --> 00:06:00.701
Colin Quinn.
"Small Talk" premieres --

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:04.000
The previews start tomorrow
at the Lucille Lortel Theatre

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.734
here in New York City.
The one and only.

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.367
We'll be right back
with a performance

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:10.634
from Madison Cunningham.
Stick around, everybody.

